## Final Judgement
The fact-check reveals that on October 8, 2020, two Chinese diplomats allegedly gatecrashed a Taiwanese event at a hotel in Suva, Fiji, and physically assaulted a Taiwanese official, resulting in hospitalization. This account comes from Taiwan’s foreign ministry and was reported by multiple news outlets (France24, Washington Post, The Guardian, etc.). However, the Chinese Embassy in Suva issued a denial, claiming its diplomats were attacked and that the reports are “totally inconsistent with the facts.” The Fijian government made no official statement, and police investigated a complaint by Chinese embassy staff against a Taiwanese employee. No independent photographic or video evidence exists. Thus, there are two directly contradictory accounts: one from Taiwan (supporting the claim) and one from China (refuting it).

